{"id":"neet-2026-q138","pn":138,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Assisted reproductive technologies","q":"Choose the correct statement regarding GIFT to overcome infertility.","o":["Ova collected from a female donor are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","It is the transfer of an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce ovum but can provide suitable environment for fertilization and development.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred into the fallopian tube of an infertile female."],"c":1,"s":"GIFT is an in-vivo technique used to assist infertility.\nGIFT (Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer) transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can provide a suitable environment for fertilization and further development.\nZIFT (Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer) is an in-vitro technique in which the zygote or early embryo up to 8 blastomeres is transferred into the fallopian tube."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q147","pn":147,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods","q":"Match List I and List II\nA. Progestasert — I. Barrier made of rubber used by females\nB. Multiload 375 — II. Oral contraceptive\nC. Diaphragm — III. Hormone releasing IUD\nD. Saheli — IV. Copper releasing IUD","o":["A(III), B(IV), C(I), D(II)","A(III), B(IV), C(II), D(I)","A(IV), B(II), C(I), D(III)","A(IV), B(III), C(I), D(II)"],"c":0,"s":"Progestasert is a hormone releasing IUD.\nMultiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.\nDiaphragm is a barrier made of rubber used by females.\nSaheli is an oral contraceptive."},
{"id":"neet-2026r-q171","pn":171,"y":"Re-NEET 2026 · 21 Jun","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Assisted reproductive technologies","q":"The method of directly of injecting a sperm into ovum in assisted reproductive technology is called:","o":["Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)","Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI)","Embryo transfer (ET)","Gamete intra fallopian transfer (GIFT)"],"c":1,"s":"ICSI is a procedure to form an embryo in the laboratory in which a sperm is injected directly into the ovum.\nZIFT transfers the zygote or early embryo (up to 8 blastomeres) into the fallopian tube.\nGIFT transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can give a suitable environment for fertilisation and development."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q093","pn":93,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Assisted reproductive technologies, IVF","q":"What are the potential drawbacks in adoption of the IVF method?\nA. High fatality risk to mother\nB. Expensive instruments and reagents\nC. Husband/wife necessary for being donors\nD. Less adoption of orphans\nE. Not available in India\nF. Possibility that the early embryo does not survive\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["B, D, F only","A, C, D, F only","A, B, C, D only","A, B, C, E, F only"],"c":0,"s":"Statements B, D and F are correct.\nStatements A, C and E are incorrect.\nHusband/wife is not necessary for being donors. IVF is available in India."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q152","pn":152,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods (IUDs)","q":"Match List I with List II :\nA. Non-medicated IUD — I. Multiload 375\nB. Copper releasing IUD — II. Progestogens\nC. Hormone releasing IND — III. Lippes loop\nD. Implants — IV. LNG-20\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-I, B-III, C-IV, D-II"],"c":1,"s":"Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.\nMultiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.\nLNG-20 is a hormone releasing IUD.\nProgestogens are used as implants.\nSo A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II."},
{"id":"neet-2024-q175","pn":175,"y":"NEET 2024 · 5 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods","q":"Which of the following is not a natural/traditional contraceptive method?","o":["Lactational amenorrhea","Vaults","Coitus interruptus","Periodic abstinence"],"c":1,"s":"Option (2) is correct.\nA vault is a rubber barrier method placed in the female tract to cover the cervix during coitus.\nLactational amenorrhea is natural: ovulation and cycles do not occur during intense lactation after childbirth.\nCoitus interruptus is natural: the male withdraws before ejaculation.\nPeriodic abstinence is natural: couples avoid coitus in the fertile period."},
{"id":"neet-2023-q152","pn":152,"y":"NEET 2023 · 7 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"RCH programme and amniocentesis","q":"Given below are two statement : one is labeled as Assertion A and the other is labeled as Reason R.\nAssertion A : Amniocentesis for sex determination is one of the strategies of Reproductive and Child Health Care Programme.\nReason R : Ban on amniocentesis checks increasing menace of female foeticide.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.","o":["A is false but R is true.","Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true and R is NOT the correct explanation of A.","A is true but R is false"],"c":0,"s":"The RCH programme spreads awareness about reproduction and gives facilities and support for a reproductively healthy society.\nAmniocentesis is used to test for genetic disorders such as Down's syndrome and haemophilia, and to judge whether the foetus can survive.\nIt is not a sex determination method in India and not an RCH strategy, so A is false.\nR is true: the ban on it checks female foeticide."},
{"id":"neet-2023-q168","pn":168,"y":"NEET 2023 · 7 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Sexually transmitted infections","q":"Which one of the following common sexually transmitted diseases is completely curable when detected early and treated properly ?","o":["HIV Infection","Genital herpes","Gonorrhoea","Hepatitis-B"],"c":2,"s":"Apart from hepatitis-B, genital herpes and HIV infection, other STIs are completely curable if found early and treated well.\nGonorrhoea is bacterial and can be cured.\nThe other three are viral."},
{"id":"neet-2023-q185","pn":185,"y":"NEET 2023 · 7 May","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods","q":"Match List I with List II.\nList I: A. Vasectomy; B. Coitus interruptus; C. Cervical caps; D. Saheli\nList II: I. Oral method; II. Barrier method; III. Surgical method; IV. Natural method\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A-IV, B-II, C-I, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV"],"c":2,"s":"Vasectomy is a surgical method.\nCoitus interruptus is a natural method.\nCervical cap is a barrier method.\nSaheli is an oral, non-steroidal pill."},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q153","pn":153,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods IUDs","q":"Which of the following is not an Intra Uterine Device?","o":["Progestasert","Progestogens","Multiload 375","Lippes loop"],"c":1,"s":"IUDs are of three kinds.\nNon-medicated: Lippes loop.\nCopper releasing: CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375.\nHormone releasing: Progestasert, LNG-20.\nProgestogens are hormones, not a device."},
{"id":"neet-2022-q172","pn":172,"y":"NEET 2022 · 17 Jul","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Intrauterine devices","q":"Lippe's loop is a type of contraceptive used as:","o":["Vault barrier","Non-Medicated IUD","Copper releasing IUD","Cervical barrier"],"c":1,"s":"Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.\nCopper-releasing IUDs are CuT, Cu7 and multiload 375.\nDiaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are barrier methods."},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q193","pn":193,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraceptive methods: IUDs","q":"IUDs are small objects made up of plastic or copper that are inserted in the uterine cavity. Which of the following statements are correct about IUDs?\n(a) IUDs decrease phagocytosis of sperm within the uterus.\n(b) The released copper ions suppress the sperm motility.\n(c) IUDs do not make the cervix hostile to the sperm.\n(d) IUDs suppress the fertilization capacity of sperm.\n(e) The IUDs require surgical intervention for their insertion in the uterine cavity.\nChoose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:","o":["(d) only","(a), (d) and (e) only","(b) and (c) only","(b) and (d) only"],"c":3,"s":"A doctor or trained nurse inserts an IUD through the vagina; no surgery is needed, so (e) is false.\nIUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm, so (a) is false.\nThey make the cervix hostile to sperm, so (c) is false.\nCopper ions reduce sperm motility and fertilising capacity, so (b) and (d) are true."},
{"id":"neet-2022-q200","pn":200,"y":"NEET 2022 · 17 Jul","tp":"Reproductive Health","st":"Contraception methods","q":"Match List – I with List – II with respect to methods of contraception and their respective actions. (a) Diaphragms (b) Contraceptive Pills (c) Intra Uterine Devices (d) Lactational Amenorrhea ; (i) Inhibit ovulation and implantation (ii) Increase phagocytosis of sperm within Uterus (iii) Absence of Menstural cycle and ovulation following parturition (iv) They cove the cervix blocking the entry of sperms","o":["(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (ii), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (ii), (b) - (iv), (c) - (i), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (iii), (b) - (ii), (c) - (i), (d) - (iv)","(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (iii), (d) - (ii)"],"c":0,"s":"Diaphragms are barriers that cover the cervix and block sperm entry.\nPills (progestogen or progestogen with oestrogen) inhibit ovulation and implantation and thicken cervical mucus.\nIUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm in the uterus.\nLactational amenorrhoea: no ovulation or periods during intense lactation after childbirth.\nSo a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii."}
